rld serpent emerging caused the sea  levels to lower and reveal a temple of  tear that was previously submersed here  we meet Brock again and shortly after  his brother sindri who reveals kratos's  wife was called a fey the passage to the  mountain is blocked by a black mist that  can only be dispelled by the light of  alfheim and so to continue on to the  mountain Kratos and atreus must travel  to alfheim the nine Norse worlds all  exist in the same place at the same time  each world has a tower that can be  accessed from tears Temple with the  bifrost bridge using a rune specific to  that realm in alfheim we see the  remnants of a war between the light and  dark elves a few thousand dark elf kills  later the light is retrieved and the  black mist from earlier is dispelled we  end up on a Mountaintop where we once  again see Boulder this time accompanied  by the sons of Thor Modi and magni they  inquire about Kratos and where they can  find him however the man being  questioned seems more interested in  insulting them than helping when they  leave Kratos decides to have a  conversation with the one-eyed man who  is entangled in a tree this man is mimir  the smartest man alive who informs crate  or senatraeus the highest peak in all  the Realms is not in midgard rather  jotenheim mimir offers to help find the  Rune that would unlock the bridge to  yotenheim however he is bound to the the  tree and no weapon can free him so  Kratos has to cut off his head the plan  is to have the witch in the woods  reanimate his head and despite the risk  mimir is more than happy to be free of  Odin's torture either way back in  freya's home she is able to reanimate  mimir using what she refers to as old  magic we now have our new companion  mimir the talking head who in my opinion  is the best addition to the franchise  while searching for a magical chisel  capable of carving the yotun roon needed  to open the bridge Kratos and atreus  finally encounter Modi and magni  needless to 